{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Embodied Intelligence.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Embodied Intelligence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"embodied intelligence embodied intelligence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Embodied Intelligence.md","fileName":"Embodied Intelligence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Embodied Intelligence","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Futures and Human Identity]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Embodied Intelligence.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Embodied Intelligence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"embodied intelligence embodied intelligence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Embodied Intelligence.md","fileName":"Embodied Intelligence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Embodied Intelligence","heading":"Embodied Intelligence","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Embodied intelligence is the view that intelligent action depends on having a body that perceives and acts within a material environment. Knowledge is not exhausted by stored propositions or formal rules; it also develops through situated coping, movement, and practical engagement.\n\nThis view challenges accounts of intelligence as abstract symbol processing alone. A machine can manipulate representations without sharing the bodily needs, vulnerabilities, and practical situations that give human concepts relevance. Embodiment does not prove that intelligent machines are impossible, but it changes the design question from reproducing detached reasoning to coordinating perception, action, environment, and learned skill.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Futures and Human Identity","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,